# backend-gauntlet — Cursor rules

This is a **LEARNING repo**. The owner is strengthening backend + scale skills by
implementing infrastructure primitives themselves, in Python. The full project
conventions live in `CLAUDE.md` at the repo root — read it.

## Hard rule: do not solve the exercises
Projects are scaffolded with `raise NotImplementedError` markers and a `SPEC.md`
"ticket". **Do NOT implement those bodies or solve SPEC challenges unless explicitly
asked.** Default to, in order: explain the concept → give graduated hints (not full
solutions) → review the user's own code → scaffold structure only.
`NotImplementedError` at runtime is by design, not a bug to fix.

## Conventions
- uv workspace: every project and `packages/common-*` is an explicit member of the
  root `pyproject.toml`; the single root `uv.lock` is committed. uv only — never pip.
- `packages/common-*` are fully-implemented shared helpers (the exception to the rule
  above) — reuse them for telemetry (`common_telemetry`) and config (`common_config`).
- Each `projects/NN-name/SPEC.md` is two-axis: Vertical (Vx internals to build from
  scratch) + Horizontal checklist (protocols/caching/security/observability). No spoilers.
- src layout `src/<package>/`: `main.py` (wiring), `config.py`, `errors.py`,
  `routes.py`, `state.py`, one module per vertical.
- Errors are exceptions: raise `AppError` subclasses; `errors.py` maps them to HTTP.
- SQL is always parameterized; never string-concatenate SQL.
- Never log secrets/API keys; never commit `.env` (gitignored).
- Idiomatic async Python (asyncio/FastAPI); pyright strict and ruff clean; match
  surrounding style.

## Useful commands
`make setup` · `make hooks` (once per clone — ruff gate on commit/push) ·
`make preflight` · `make status`. Per project: `make verify`, `make run`,
`docker compose up -d`.
